  "description": "GUHRIM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H161 Cr4 N9 Nd4 O37,C2 H3 N1,7(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr4 (Cr) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.431-4.511 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.91-125.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C82H161Cr4N9Nd4O37·MeCN·7CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
